{
  "run_id": "PMC10920630__expert_context__pcd_nodecider_PCD_o3mini__s1",
  "auditor": "trapi:gpt-5.6-sol_2026-07-09",
  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "The starting material is Q235 low-carbon steel in the as-received state.",
      "field": "material_initial_state",
      "needs_support": false,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Q235 samples will be annealed in air at 700 °C for 1, 3, or 6 hours.",
      "field": "intervention",
      "needs_support": false,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Annealing Q235 in air at 700 °C will form a uniform oxide scale.",
      "field": "intervention",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The thermally grown scale on Q235 will consist primarily of Fe2O3 and Fe3O4, with minor alloying-element oxides or spinels.",
      "field": "structural_mediator",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The thickness, uniformity, continuity, and adhesion of the thermally grown scale govern its protective behavior.",
      "field": "structural_mediator",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC10488378::web::013::3_3_hot_corrosion_behavior"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "A uniform, adherent oxide scale acts as a barrier to salt infiltration and subsequent oxidation or reaction.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC10488378::web::013::3_3_hot_corrosion_behavior",
        "PMC10488378::web::014::3_3_hot_corrosion_behavior"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "A defective or nonuniform scale permits salt access and initiates localized corrosion.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC10488378::web::013::3_3_hot_corrosion_behavior",
        "PMC10488378::web::014::3_3_hot_corrosion_behavior"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "Pre-oxidized Q235 with a continuous scale will undergo less high-temperature corrosion-related mass change than untreated Q235.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC10488378::web::013::3_3_hot_corrosion_behavior"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "Pre-oxidized Q235 with a continuous scale will exhibit less localized corrosion than untreated Q235 during high-temperature salt exposure.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC10488378::web::013::3_3_hot_corrosion_behavior",
        "PMC10488378::web::014::3_3_hot_corrosion_behavior"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "The high-temperature tests will use 75% Na2SO4 plus 25% NaCl at 700–900 °C.",
      "field": "conditions",
      "needs_support": false,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC10488378::web::013::3_3_hot_corrosion_behavior",
        "PMC10488378::web::014::3_3_hot_corrosion_behavior"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "Pre-oxidized and untreated Q235 should perform similarly in a mild saline solution at room temperature.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "At room temperature, the preformed passive oxide is stable and its protective role is less critical.",
      "field": "boundary",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The proposed oxide-scale mechanism applies when pre-oxidation produces a uniform layer without significantly changing the underlying Q235 microstructure.",
      "field": "boundary",
      "needs_support": false,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Annealing may alter grain size or phase composition and thereby independently influence corrosion behavior.",
      "field": "boundary",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Failure of pre-oxidized Q235 to show a statistically significant reduction in mass loss or improved scale integrity relative to untreated Q235 at high temperature would falsify the proposed primary oxide-barrier explanation.",
      "field": "falsification_experiment",
      "needs_support": false,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    }
  ],
